      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "REGISTER YOUR INTEREST NOW\r\n\r\nRaistin Court is a charming new homes development located in the townland of Clonmellon, Co. Westmeath. The development has 26 A-Rated residential homes offering a mix of 2 and 3 bed houses. These beautifully designed Energy Rated homes are ideal for first time buyers or downsizers. Each home in Raistin Court is finished to a high standard. Raistin Court is within walking distance to a variety of amenities such as shops, church, national school, community hall and Sporting amenities.\r\n\r\nRaistin Court is within a short drive to the prestigious Killua Castle, a historic castle with links to Sir Walter Raleigh and Lawrence of Arabia. It also offers a unique dining experience within its award winning Twelve Points restaurant. The beautiful St. Johns Church is opened to the public and is ideal for walks within the area. Other local attractions within a short drive are Loughcrew Megalithic Centre, Loughcrew Cairns, Fore Abbey, Mullaghmeen Forest, Spire of Lloyd, Lough Lene, Lough Sheelin and Lough Ramor.\r\n\r\nLocation\r\nClonmellon was built in the late eighteenth century by Sir Benjamin Chapman. By 1837 Clonmellon was established as a market town. There is a monthly market that takes place one Sunday a month. It's located in the Old Market Square and is an ideal location for visitors to wander from stall to stall.\r\n\r\nClonmellon is very well positioned on the Westmeath / Meath border and benefits from being within a 10km proximity to the M3 motorway (Kells south exit) that provides direct access to Navan, Blanchardstown, Dublin and the M50. Clonmellon also offers easy access to Mullingar via the N52."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Brand new 2 and 3 bedroom houses\r\nBER A2 Rated - Eligible for Green Mortgages\r\nEnergy Efficient air to heat systems\r\nTriple Glazed Windows\r\nWithin close proximity to the N3 & N52 - giving access to Navan, Dublin, M50 and Mullingar\r\nGranite Windowsills"
      }
    ],
